  "body": "**Stacked on #715** (grblHAL post, not merged yet): this branch is #715's head plus one commit, so the diff shows #715's files too until it merges. Only commit `feat(machines): Sienci AltMill ...` is this PR. Fork synced at v0.16.0 (via #715's base).\n\n## What changed\n\nThree built-in machines for Sienci's AltMill routers, which run grblHAL on the SLB-EXT controller. They post through the existing `grblhal.cps`; there is no AltMill post file.\n\n- `assets/machines/sienci-altmill-2x4.mch`, `-4x4.mch` and `-4x8.mch`, registered in `posting::MACHINES` as \"Sienci AltMill 2x4\", \"4x4\" and \"4x8\".\n- **Units mm, 3 axes.** The Vortex rotary waits on #714.\n- **`safe_retract: 0.0`.** The AltMill homes (`$22=79`: homing on, required at startup, machine origin 0 at home; Z homes up; soft limits on). So every tool change lifts `G53 G0 Z0`, then `T<n> M6` stands alone. gSender and ncSender take over on `T<n> M6` (manual change, RapidChange or Sienci ATC), so the post needs no ATC or manual mode and no rack list.\n- **Figures** from Sienci's spec pages. The 4x4's travel (1260 x 1248 x 170 mm soft limits), axis rates and spindle range (1200-24000 rpm) are read from a 4x4's own `$$`. Every figure and its source is in `docs/decisions/728-altmill.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\n- New `altmill_machines.rs` (4 tests): each file's figures; the `G53 G0 Z0` lift before each `T<n> M6` and no G43/G43.1/G49; a spindle speed past 24000 refused; the 4x4 two-tool program locked byte-exact in mm and inch (`golden/nc/grblhal/altmill_4x4_two_tool{,_inch}.nc`).\n- Green on macOS: `altmill_machines`, `machine` (the library list now pins the three), `machine_library`, `machine_edit`, `conformance`, `grblhal_post`, `tormach_machines`. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test altmill_machines -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n- **Machine run:** the 4x4 golden air-cut on an AltMill 4x4 (SLB-EXT) with ncSender and an 8-pocket RapidChange ATC; the `T3 M6` and `T4 M6` changes ran cleanly (comment below).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The 2x4 and 4x8 figures come from Sienci's pages only; an owner's `$$` would confirm them.\n- Full workspace gate not run (disk-limited machine); the suites above are the ones that touch the machine registry and the grblHAL post.\n\nChangelog: Sienci AltMill 2x4, 4x4 and 4x8 machines, posting through the grblHAL post (#728)\n\nFixes #728\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
